Backport gnulib commit c44fe03b72 "string-h: Fix compilation error on macOS
with fortify." to every bundled copy of string.in.h in gettext 0.25.1.
https://github.com/coreutils/gnulib/commit/c44fe03b72
https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?67300

The ISO C N3322 block (GCC >= 15 only) redeclares memcpy, strndup, strncmp,
... unconditionally. glibc < 2.26 (e.g. sysroot 2.17) defines strndup and
strncmp as __extension__ macros in <bits/string2.h> when optimizing, so the
redeclarations fail with "expected identifier or '(' before '__extension__'".

